\f1\fs22 After Solo\'92s visit, Tony cheered up. We\'92d like to report that his sunnier disposition was due entirely to Solo\'92s inspirational exhortations; certainly the prospect Tony would reunite with Sarah in the future buoyed him back to the shallows of his good humour. Solo 
\f2\i did
\f1\i0  say it would be soon, didn\'92t he? However, having reviewed other, more substantial evidence available, we believe the root cause of Tony\'92s improved mood lay with the frequency and number of groupies he was fucking.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony woke to the sound of birds singing from ruined rooftops and entangled power lines. His first thought, as he blinked his eyelashes unglued: the ceiling was the cleanest he\'92d ever slept under. In one outstretched hand, he still held a bottle of Livid Emu whiskey; the other was pinned under Betty Lee, one of the growing number of Elvisettes who made sure his every whim was catered for, except for every time he whimsically ordered to be left the tax alone.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony was beginning to understand how suffocated Sarah must have felt cloistered in the mansion. If the Elvi attributed saintliness to the Holy Momma, they were ascribing the base bacchanalian appetites of a devil to him. The men loved drinking with him, and women loved \'85 well they loved very well, thank you very much. Which mostly suited Tony just fine, if only he had a single moment\'92s peace to himself once in a while.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony delicately tried to extract his arm out from under Betty Lee. She moaned and rolled away, which gave him opportunity to slide free. He haunched up on his elbow, drained the dregs of whiskey, and let the bottle slide to the floor behind.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>As his eyes toured like a slow-moving Cadillac around the curves and corners of Betty Lee\'92s naked body and the bodies of Marguerita and Princess Shalimar who were asleep and snuggled behind her, Tony marvelled as he realised how they appeared more beautiful to him with each passing day. As his traced his finger over the smooth satin skin of Betty Lee\'92s hip, he thought, 
\f2\i Is this love?
\f1\i0  and admitted to himself he wouldn\'92t have a clue. He\'92d never been in love before, unless he counted the forlorn infatuations for Airborne girls he\'92d indulged in since he was a boy. If not love, then why was he no longer noticing the physical imperfections of his bed companions. As much as he squinted or widened his eyes, he could no longer see the crow\'92s feet by Betty Lee\'92s eyes, nor the first signs of grey in her hair, nor the cellulite on her hips, nor even the the little roll of fat he was sure she sported the first time he saw her unclothed. He could see no such imperfection in Marguerita and Princess Shalimar, either. What was this? Had his boyhood fantasies of winning a woman above his station poisoned his mind so much? Had he developed such a neurotic distaste for any girl who was interested in him he saw flaws they never possessed?\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>As if scalded, he sharply withdrew his hand away from Betty Lee; he\'92d been writing 
\f2\i Sarah
\f1\i0  repeatedly on her butt.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony rose and, on his way to the bathroom, almost tripped over a naked Elvisette sleeping on the floor at the foot of the bed. His tip-toeing around her failed when another infatuated fan leaped out of the closet and hollered, \'91Surprise.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony jumped with fright, and the sleeping Elvisette roused. Betty Lee woke quickly, vaulted over Marguerita and Princess Shalimar, squared up to the invader. With a military snap she pointed at the door and ordered, \'91Out.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The invader\'92s shoulders slumped. \'91Can I just get an autograph?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony smiled, Betty Lee relented. The invader pulled a marking pen from her jeans pocket, offered it to Tony, and unbuttoned her blouse. Tony signed over her collar bone while Betty Lee looked on like an unimpressed overseer and the other three snuggled on the bed.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Singing could be heard from the balcony. A half dozen Elvisettes huddled close to the glass doors, singing 
\f2\i Evolve me Tender
\f1\i0 .\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91How\'92d they get up here?\'92 Betty Lee asked, disbelieving.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>One of the singers held up a grappling hook and a heavy rope. Tony was amused; they\'92d got some of the lyrics wrong, but Tony thought substituting \'91love\'92 for \'91evolve\'92 was possibly an improvement. He threw open the doors.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91You\'92re not letting them in,\'92 Betty Lee shrieked.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Nah,\'92 Tony answered. \'91But they deserve autographs too.\'92 He twiddled the marker still in his hand and retrieved a note pad. The Elvisettes outside stopped singing and shrieked with joy as Tony scribbled and handed out pages.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>One of the singers beheld her new trophy with adoration which quickly turned to confusion and scorn. \'91Who is Tony Supaporn? We want the Great Teacher.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>After showering, Tony relented and dressed in the jumpsuit that had been specially designed and crafted for the Great Teacher.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91There\'92s too much gold in it,\'92 he complained to Princess Shalimar as he zipped up. His complaint was about both the colour and the material. Real gold thread was woven into the fabric, and it reflected light in unpredictable, vision-impairing ways. Tony almost blinded himself when he turned the light on during his last bathroom visit, and only staved off blindness by grabbing a pair of sunglasses someone had left by the sink and shoving them firmly on the bridge of his nose.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>He refused to wear the poncho.\

